{"error":false,"activeTest":false,"task":{"id":14228209,"type":"Review","status":"Processing","importance":1,"reason":null,"locked":null,"proofId":null,"currentQuestionId":null,"currentQuestionTimestamp":null,"progress":1,"points":4,"passed":1,"rawPointsAwarded":4,"pointsAwarded":4,"mp":null,"mpAwarded":null,"mpDecayRate":null,"student":{"id":57975,"firstName":"Harrison","lastName":"Charles","locale":null,"subscriptionId":"sub_1UO3yHD4gcTFRx97dYjQXmX1","sequenceId":19},"course":{"id":111,"name":"Mathematical Foundations II"},"topic":{"id":673,"name":"Sigma Notation"},"test":{"id":null,"name":null,"diagnostic":null,"timeLimit":null,"questionCount":null},"created":"2026-10-15T05:11:42.000Z","started":"2026-10-15T05:43:37.000Z","completed":"2026-10-15T05:44:29.000Z","processed":null,"progressStr":"100%","answers":[{"id":62200560,"created":"2026-10-15T05:43:52.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":2,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15801,"number":1,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 5:43 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:16","question":{"id":5338,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":4166,"text":"<p>Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^3 5\\cdot2^{n-1}.$</p>\n","choice1":"$35$","choice2":"$20$","choice3":"$25$","choice4":"$40$","choice5":"$45$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>The sum takes integer values of $n$ from $1$ to $3.$ So, computing the terms for $n=1,2,3$ and then adding them, we get</p>\n<p>\\[\n\t\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^3 5\\cdot2^{n-1}&=\\big(5\\cdot2^{1-1}\\big)+\\big(5\\cdot2^{2-1}\\big)+\\big(5\\cdot2^{3-1}\\big)\\\\[-5pt]\n                 &=\\big(5\\cdot2^{0}\\big)+\\big(5\\cdot2^{1}\\big)+\\big(5\\cdot2^{2}\\big)\\\\[5pt]\n                 &=(5\\cdot 1)+(5\\cdot 2)+(5\\cdot 4)\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&=5 + 10 + 20 \\\\[5pt]\n\t\t&=35.\n\t}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":673,"name":"Sigma Notation"},"example":{"id":4166,"title":"Evaluating Expressions Written in Sigma Notation"},"group":{"id":80136,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14228209,"answer":{"id":62200560,"cread":"2026-10-15T05:43:52.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":2,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15801},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62200583,"created":"2026-10-15T05:44:09.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11471,"number":2,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 5:44 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:11","question":{"id":66995,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":4168,"text":"<p>Express $S=8+16+24+\\cdots+80+88$ in sigma notation.</p>\n","choice1":"$\\displaystyle{\\sum_{n=1}^{11} 8n}$","choice2":"$\\displaystyle{\\sum_{n=1}^{11} (n+8)}$","choice3":"$\\displaystyle{\\sum_{n=1}^{11} (8n+8)}$","choice4":"$\\displaystyle{\\sum_{n=1}^{11} (8n-8)}$","choice5":"$\\displaystyle{\\sum_{n=1}^{10} 8n}$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>Notice that the terms of the corresponding sequence</p>\n<p>\\[\n8, \\quad 16, \\quad 24, \\quad  \\ldots, \\quad 80, \\quad 88.\n\\]\n are multiples of $8,$ and since $88\\div 8= 11,$ there are $11$ terms in total. </p>\n<p>Therefore, the $n$th term of the sequence has the form\n\\[\na_n =8n,\n\\]\nwhere $n$ ranges from $n=1$ to $n=11.$ Indeed: </p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\na_1 &= 8(1)  =8 \\\\[5pt]\na_2 &=8(2)  =16 \\\\[5pt]\na_3 &=8(3)  =24 \\\\\n& \\:\\:\\vdots \\\\[3pt]\na_{10} &= 8(10)  = 80 \\\\[5pt]\na_{11} &= 8(11) =88 \\\\\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>Therefore,</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\eqalign{\nS=8+16+24+\\cdots+80+88=\\sum_{n=1}^{11} 8n.\n}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":673,"name":"Sigma Notation"},"example":{"id":4168,"title":"Writing Sums Using Sigma Notation"},"group":{"id":80142,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14228209,"answer":{"id":62200583,"cread":"2026-10-15T05:44:09.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11471},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62200624,"created":"2026-10-15T05:44:29.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":"[\"\\\\frac{16}{5}\"]","timeElapsed":16138,"number":3,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 5:44 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:16","question":{"id":251017,"format":"FR","difficulty":3,"exampleId":4166,"text":"Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\sum_{m=2}^5\\dfrac{2m+1}{10}=$","choice1":" ","choice2":" ","choice3":" ","choice4":" ","choice5":" ","freeAnswerChoice":"[\n    answer: \\dfrac{16}{5};\n    type: number;\n    width: 35;\n    margin-left: 4;\n    margin-right: 1;\n    buttons: frac;\n]","explanation":"<p>The sum takes integer values of $m$ from $2$ to $5.$ So, computing the terms for $m=2,3,4,5$ and then adding them, we get\n\\begin{align*}\n\\displaystyle\\sum_{m=2}^5\\dfrac{2m+1}{10}\n&=\\dfrac{2\\cdot2+1}{10}+\\dfrac{2\\cdot3+1}{10}\n+\\dfrac{2\\cdot4+1}{10}+\\dfrac{2\\cdot5+1}{10}\\\\[-2pt]\n&=\\dfrac{5}{10}+\\dfrac{7}{10}+\\dfrac{9}{10}+\\dfrac{11}{10}\\\\[7pt] \n&=\\dfrac{5+7+9+11}{10}\\\\[5pt] \n&=\\dfrac{32}{10}\\\\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac{\\cancel{2}\\cdot 16} {\\cancel{2}\\cdot 5} \\\\[5pt]\n&=\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{\\dfrac{16}{5}}. \n\\end{align*}</p>\n","topic":{"id":673,"name":"Sigma Notation"},"example":{"id":4166,"title":"Evaluating Expressions Written in Sigma Notation"},"group":{"id":80139,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14228209,"answer":{"id":62200624,"cread":"2026-10-15T05:44:29.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":["\\frac{16}{5}"],"timeElapsed":16138},"graphic":false,"freeResponse":{"segments":[{"textbox":{"answer":"\\dfrac{16}{5}","type":"number","width":35,"margin":{"left":4,"right":1},"buttons":["frac"]}}]},"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false